  <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted leading-relaxed">
    <p>Tax Deducted at Source (TDS) is the foundational collection engine of the Indian direct tax architecture. Designed under the <strong>Income-tax Act, 1961</strong> to capture taxes at the exact point of income generation, TDS operates on the "pay as you earn" principle. Payers (deductors) are legally mandated to withhold a specified percentage before disbursing payments to contractors, professionals, landlords, and commercial vendors, remitting the balance to the central government.</p>

    <p>For corporate finance teams, startup founders, and chartered accountants, staying updated on shifting statutory thresholds, differential rates for technical versus professional services under <strong>Section 194J</strong>, and punitive withholding rates for non-filers under <strong>Section 206AB</strong> is non-negotiable. Falling afoul of TDS provisions triggers mandatory disallowance of business expenses under Section 40(a)(ia), punitive monthly interest, and daily late-filing fees.</p>

    <!-- Key Takeaway Box -->
    <div class="my-6 rounded-2xl border-2 border-primary/20 bg-primary/[0.03] p-6 dark:border-primary/30 dark:bg-primary/[0.05]">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-primary inline-block"></span>
        Core TDS Rule Summary (FY 2025-26)
      </h3>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-body dark:text-muted">
        <strong>Technical services (FTS) under 194J are taxed at 2%, while professional services remain at 10%.</strong> Contractor payments under 194C are taxed at <strong>1% (individual)</strong> or <strong>2% (corporate)</strong> once aggregate billings cross ₹1,00,000. Rent on immovable property under 194I is taxed at <strong>10%</strong> above the ₹2,40,000 annual threshold.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-8">Master TDS Rate Chart for FY 2025-26 (AY 2026-27)</h2>
    <p><strong>The Income Tax Department enforces specific withholding rates and exemption thresholds across different payment categories under Chapter XVII-B of the Act.</strong> The master reference table below details the statutory rates applicable for the current financial year:</p>

